 "note": "Compare to the start HEAD: SessionStart records the work tree's HEAD in the session's start record (head, null outside git), and `risk` ends the test/build exemption once a test or build definition differs between that start HEAD and HEAD, so a commit, a fast-forward merge, a checkout or a reset counts like a work-tree edit; a rename counts under both names; a resumed session keeps its oldest record's HEAD; a commit that changes no build file keeps the exemption. An unknown start HEAD asks: no record of the session for that work tree, an anonymous session, a record without a head, a commit git does not have. An own command is unaffected. MITIGATIONS 4.1: a git status or start-HEAD diff that fails, runs out of time or is cut off at 4 MiB asks (it read as nothing changed). Stated limit: the start HEAD is per session id, so a successor (clear, fork, handoff-resume) starts on its own HEAD (the last steps). Review r2: the start HEAD is the oldest along clear and handoff-resume links (ctx::chain), so a manual /clear no longer re-arms the exemption; a fork starts on its own HEAD (the stated limit). A jobs.jsonl record never lifts a test_build_re run that fails a check, and lifts no command while a test or build definition changed, the start HEAD is unknown or git cannot tell. A Makefile or package.json git does not track (an ignored folder) defines no target.",
